      objectReference: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8950ef15c887d534a8f622603f1ddebc, type: 3}
    - target: {fileID: 1349625746, guid: 08fe3cfc2cba1c444a207853146ad202, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "Murdoch Active is holding an eSports day for high school students to
        come through as a kind of open day for the uni, obviously with a more tailored
        angle of studying games. The official event runs from 9-12:15. There will
        be 3 groups of students cycling through the day. Each group gets a 10 minute
        presentation and then a roughly 20 minute walk around to some of the activities.
        We will be set up in room 360.4.031 (the room just above the main entrance)
        with some laptops supplied by the eSports team to run some demos of student
        made games.\r\nYour job would basically be to come before 9, set your game
        up on the laptop - which I can help with! - and then enjoy watching students
        play your game and provide feedback. From my own experience in showing off
        my game demos these events are always great. Both in getting some feedback
        and that warm fuzzy feeling of seeing people enjoy your game \U0001F605 \r\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
